In Ann Arbor, when I lived there several years ago, parking enforcement was
basically a legalized extortion scheme run by the city in collusion with
several of the major tow truck operators.  For all I know, it may still be.

A tactic which a number of folks adopted (I won't say if I was one of them :-)
was to pop a quarter into the meter any time they encountered a car with an
expired meter *and* a parking ticket on the windshield.  The driver of the car
would return to find themselves ticketed with time still on the meter.  This
proved decidedly unhelpful to the public credibility of the parking police.

