From: "Brady, Mark" <mbrady@msmail.his.tch.tmc.edu>
Date: Wed, 27 Jul 94 07:43:00 PDT
Subject: [#94-7-225] Spontaneous anti-govt. outbreak in D.C.

Having lived in the DC area for twelve years, the only thing that the DC 
government does efficiently is ticket and tow vehicles.  Yes, it is illegal 
to feed the meter, you can get an additional ticket for that, eventhough it 
is not your vehicle (although I have never heard of the law being enforced). 
 In addition, because traffic is so bad (#2 after New York City per National 
Geographic August 1994 issue) many roads do not allow parking during rush 
hours so all vehicles are towed as soon as rush hour begins.  The DC police 
can tow your vehicle in about 15 seconds.
Someone mentioned that this was legalized extortion.  Yes, it is but then 
isn't that what government is all about.  The policy was started by Marion 
"I was setup" Barry in an effort to generate revenue.  It is supported by 
the people of DC because a significant number of vehicles ticketed are from 
outside of the District.  In addition, Congress has not allowed DC to pass a 
commuting tax, so the DC government has attempted to do this by other means 
(Congress is exempt from parking tickets).  However, this has pretty much 
killed the downtown shopping districts plans to have night hours, who wants 
to put up with this when you can shop in a suburban mall (although some, 
like Clarendon, now charge you to park and shop).  Finally, because DC 
parking rates are so high ($300/month and up), people will risk feeding the 
meter and getting the occasional $50 ticket.  Good reason to move to Texas, 
I say.

